From: Anargyros Plemenos <anargyros.plemenos@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:25:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Use MLflow for model signatures, the model registry and agent
 tracing

- Log every model with a signature and input example; the service checks
  each champion's signature against the features it computes and refuses
  to start on a mismatch.
- Replace the hand-made current.json pointer with the MLflow Model
  Registry: each training run registers a new version, which becomes
  @champion only if its primary metric is not worse. The app loads
  @champion; rollback is `python -m ml.promote <model> <version>`.
- Trace every agent question in MLflow: routing decision, each Claude
  call (via anthropic autolog), each tool call with full inputs and
  outputs, tagged with mode and model versions. Responses carry trace_id.
- Models are saved with skops instead of pickle; tracking store is SQLite
  under ml/artifacts/mlflow. Upgrade mlflow to 3.17.0 and anthropic to
  1.1.0 (the autolog-supported range).
- Add registry, promotion and tracing tests (33 total), make models and
  make mlflow-ui targets, README section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
